                {
                    "type": "text",
                    "content": "Here are my top recommendations for your Paris trip, keeping your budget and preferences in mind:\n\nRestaurant (Authentic French Cuisine, Top-Rated):\n- Le Baratin\n  - Rating: 4.8\n  - Reviews: Small, cozy bistro with delicious, homestyle cooking. Daily changing menu based on fresh market ingredients. Natural wine selection. Great view of the city.\n  - Address: 3 Rue Jouye-Rouve, 75020 Paris, France\n\nOther excellent French options (if you want variety):\n- Bistrot Paul Bert (Rating: 4.5, 18 Rue Paul Bert, 75011 Paris)\n- Chez L'Ami Jean (Rating: 4.4, 27 Rue Malar, 75007 Paris)\n\nHotel (Highly-Rated, Budget-Friendly):\n- Montmartre Suites\n  - Rating: 4.7\n  - Reviews: Luxurious suites with stunning views of Montmartre. Impeccable cleanliness and attention to detail. Perfect location for exploring Montmartre. Note: The environment can be noisy, and rooms are not soundproof.\n  - Price Range: 110\u2013200 euros per night\n  - Address: 23 Rue Lepic, 75018 Paris, France\n\nAlternative (if you prefer a central location):\n- Le Marais Boutique (Rating: 4.2, 12 Rue des Archives, 75004 Paris, Price: 120\u2013180 euros/night)\n\nBoth the restaurant and hotel are highly rated and fit well within your 500-euro budget for a short stay. Let me know if you\u2019d like to make reservations or need more details!"
